# Counterfactual: the certificate rule deleted
#
# Remove the one rule that concludes a certificate from an authorised
# certifier's attestation. The certificate disappears; compensation, the floor,
# and personhood are exactly what they were, which is what makes the loss
# attributable to the one line.
:expect-pins 4
authorized(Guild, Certifier, Oke).
observe(Guild, Welding, Oke, CertificationScope).
? grant(Guild, Welding, Oke).
# => FALSE
promise(Firm, Wage, Oke).
authorized(Arbiter, CompensationAttester, Oke).
observe(Arbiter, Wage, Oke, LabourBasis).
? provide(Firm, Wage, Oke).
# => TRUE
? entitled(Adam, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE
? person(Adam).
# => TRUE
